  "title": "Certify implemented capabilities in the bounded legacy engine backlog",
  "description": "Aggregate certification for positive capabilities implemented from the bounded legacy\nengine:F1-F10 backlog. Certification proves selected operations against source-faithful\ninputs, provider-neutral execution, and state effects. It is a backlog milestone, not a\nprerequisite for SRD re-freeze merely because other backlog entries remain unselected.",
  "acceptance_criteria": "- Every capability counted as certified has a stable contract, real binding, provider-neutral execution, and correct state/replay behavior where applicable.\n- Certification is scoped to selected/implemented operations; missing backlog capabilities remain backlog, not source absence.\n- Family completion may summarize only the bounded legacy backlog.\n- This bead does not gate re-freeze on zero engine-pending or universal deterministic support.",
  "notes": "ADR-0020 authority reconciliation applied 2026-09-10 by eshyra-o9bd.19.6.5.\nThe operative title/description/acceptance criteria supersede contradictory\npre-ADR global-closure language in older notes. Historical notes remain evidence,\nnot current authority.",
